="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="3FC8A089" w:rsidR="312E7155"><w:t>Where is the start of this sentence?</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="MK" w:author="Maggie Khoushi" w:date="2026-09-08T21:09:27" w:id="172747243" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="5C379DBB" w:rsidRDefault="5CFD32BE" w14:paraId="0968BA01" w14:textId="5F7448B3" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="3F968F9B" w:rsidR="6636B2D1"><w:t>its right above the table label but i agree that the table should not split the paragraph - this applies to all the tables and images in the paper, the constant cut offs mid-paragraph are really disruptive</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="AT" w:author="Annika Tekumulla" w:date="2026-09-08T21:34:07" w:id="826233184" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="133C5A53" w:rsidRDefault="3ECD3CCD" w14:paraId="0E41A682" w14:textId="6A985F6E" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="2CD128E7" w:rsidR="5F43ED96"><w:t>what about for LSTV?</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="AT" w:author="Annika Tekumulla" w:date="2026-09-08T21:35:31" w:id="1868922712" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="3AE4AE45" w:rsidRDefault="7C657B39" w14:paraId="79D4C547" w14:textId="19273AB2" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="2F86577A" w:rsidR="1174A763"><w:t>source?</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="AT" w:author="Annika Tekumulla" w:date="2026-09-08T21:36:10" w:id="284813284" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="7A854F32" w:rsidRDefault="031084F0" w14:paraId="5C7FAB10" w14:textId="7E5CA4F6" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="427969B1" w:rsidR="5D986528"><w:t>MRI? Didn't focus on this in the paper</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="MK" w:author="Maggie Khoushi" w:date="2026-09-08T22:11:40" w:id="1741837754" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="1455AF2B" w:rsidRDefault="16E2D748" w14:paraId="19FA5FCB" w14:textId="62185C7F" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="510243D0" w:rsidR="6FDD436A"><w:t>i dont think phrases in the body should be bolded or italicized, i think that would be better reserved for headings</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="MK" w:author="Maggie Khoushi" w:date="2026-09-08T22:36:22" w:id="2132209053" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="5DC4A8AB" w:rsidRDefault="1F8CEE38" w14:paraId="67519A4C" w14:textId="62387A54" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="372BDE7E" w:rsidR="179DD4D5"><w:t>applies to many other examples above and below. need to pick one and fix all the rest</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="MK" w:author="Maggie Khoushi" w:date="2026-09-08T22:16:32" w:id="291662962" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="6D3A79A3" w:rsidRDefault="2FBEEF63" w14:paraId="0E91E70E" w14:textId="6E04473B" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="464C854B" w:rsidR="257900BD"><w:t>this sentence has a random subheading and drop down menu linked to it somehow ? you can see it if you hover your pointer just left of the sentence</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="MK" w:author="Maggie Khoushi" w:date="2026-09-08T22:27:33" w:id="1934048125" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="063D00E5" w:rsidRDefault="7097A0D6" w14:paraId="31626E1B" w14:textId="213AEA8D" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="7D99EBA6" w:rsidR="39BF089D"><w:t>actually there are a lot of these randomly</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="MS" w:author="Mia Sooch" w:date="2026-09-08T22:21:56" w:id="1616041658" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="60E6848B" w:rsidRDefault="22D0BCE3" w14:paraId="7BE41CF2" w14:textId="4F43DC45" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="468979B2" w:rsidR="4390810B"><w:t xml:space="preserve">It might be helpful to add a picture so the reader's can reference what a transitional variant looks like and how it can serve as an identifier </w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="MS" w:author="Mia Sooch" w:date="2026-09-08T22:27:23" w:id="1444959721" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="05468722" w:rsidRDefault="633B32BA" w14:paraId="02A1A524" w14:textId="4767774E" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="39007C6F" w:rsidR="54AA4693"><w:t>Explain what "protocol" is. Dumb this down, can be hard to follow without background knowledge</w:t></w:r></w:p></w:comment><w:comment w:initials="MK" w:author="Maggie Khoushi" w:date="2026-09-08T22:29:11" w:id="1252928524" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:p w:rsidR="27EA1DFE" w:rsidRDefault="21C5943E" w14:paraId="19C59718" w14:textId="272C391E" xmlns:w14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/word/2010/wordml" xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main"><w:pPr><w:pStyle w:val="CommentText" /></w:pPr><w:r><w:rPr><w:rStyle w:val="CommentReference" /></w:rPr><w:annotationRef /></w:r><w:r w:rsidRPr="5907B2A2" w:rsidR="53A9B243"><w:t>not sure if this was copied from another source but there are a lot of random gaps / strange formatting gaps mid-sentence, probably just need a once over before sending to the reviewers to make sure we catch all of them. I tried to fix as m